+# Intake and bounded roadmap — 2026-09-22 Japan time
+
+## Read through GitHub MCP
+
+- main: `b2457b746a6df06f6536585dfe2ab937aff639f4`, rechecked before freeze;
+- root README; docs/CURRENT_GOAL.md governing/current sections; ROADMAP.md;
+- newest open Issue collection/search, open PR collection, branch inventory plus targeted branch search;
+- closed #916 and #926 and #926's freeze/result comments; exact #742 Git blob;
+- related open #3876 (passive event delivery boundary), #2789/#57 (integration priority), #3033 (research discipline);
+- active #3929 query-version reader overlap is a different worker allocation and remains untouched.
+
+This is a targeted intake, not an exhaustive audit of all hundreds of Issues or all branch pages. Search indexing/partial response limits are not treated as proof of absence. The intended exact main path returned 404, and branch search for `gap` returned none. No remote reservation or exclusive ownership has been established.
+
+## What is and is not available
+
+All 48 exposed GitHub MCP actions were inspected: only read operations, no Issue/comment/branch/content/PR/merge/delete write operation. Plugin-directory search returned the same installed GitHub connector, not another usable writer. Repository permissions report push/admin, but that does not create a missing tool operation.
+
+Local environment has git and Python; `gh` and `docker` are absent. Direct public GitHub request failed DNS. No credentials were searched or extracted; no attempt was made to bypass the MCP read-only interface. Publication, remote Issue preregistration, PR creation/merge, and remote branch cleanup are BLOCKED. Preserve this distinction in every report. No remote write occurred.
+
+## Local research sequence
+
+1. Reconstruct exact inherited event admission and record the new notification hypothesis.
+2. Run excluded construction and corruption tests.
+3. Freeze H/T/D/C/U, source, schedule and environment locally.
+4. Execute one 72-case process/clock allocation, retaining every raw record and database.
+5. Reconstruct independently, run corruption controls, and rehash sources.
+6. Package evidence, a successor Issue draft, PR draft and fully additive patch for another agent.
+7. Remote publication, review, integration, main readback and cleanup remain blocked; do not claim completion.
+
+## Broader repository roadmap
+
+The rich-model-intent/local-refinement objective remains. This work addresses only the interpretation of a gap notification for potential receipt delivery. It is not the matched six-task desktop experiment, O3/O4 live verification, sustained DOOM control, model/human-tempo comparison, cross-platform runtime validation or release readiness. Those retain their existing owners and prerequisites. Do not check broad roadmap boxes on the strength of this study.
+
+## Preservation
+
+Retain every predecessor result. The #926 count rule is judged against its own count contract, not retroactively against an 80 ms deadline. Local changes are confined to the intended new research path. No README/CURRENT_GOAL/ROADMAP/shared runtime or other worker files are edited. No remote branch is deleted because evidence/dependency checks and write capability are insufficient.
